cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "agent-civ-lab: Behavioral experiments on LLM-agent societies"
authors:
  - family-names: Chatterjee
    given-names: Aditya
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-13
license: MIT
keywords:
  - large language models
  - multi-agent systems
  - collusion
  - cooperation
  - game theory
  - AI safety
abstract: >
  A small, reproducible harness for measuring how LLM agents behave in
  multi-agent games: convention formation and committed-minority tipping
  (naming game), commons governance with optional enforcement (GovSim-style),
  price collusion (Bertrand duopoly), and cooperation/defection (iterated
  Prisoner's Dilemma). Includes single-sentence prompt interventions that
  causally induce collusion or early defection.
